is headquartered in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason T. Liberty | CEO & Chairman | Compensation: $8.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 107K people. Revenue per employee of $166K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $11K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 49\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $79.3B market cap on $17.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $1.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.51\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 6.2% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 76% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7556070743231839},{"