DA ($825.0M of cash against $21.3B of debt), with interest covered 4.9x.","The current ratio of 0.18 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","It runs on negative working capital (-21 days), so customers and suppliers effectively fund its operations."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 26.6% over 3 years and 52.0% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 126%).","At current returns, reinvesting 37% of profits supports about 4.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Margins are expanding (+1.1% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 4%.","Capex runs 3.0x depreciation (29.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 58, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 6.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 89%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (73 sales, net $337.3M sold).","It returns 2.5% a year to shareholders (1.5% in buybacks and 2.0% in dividends).","The share count has grown 1.0% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 107,950 employees, each generates about $166K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 6.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $11K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $8.2M (49x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":43,"head":"Watch: priced 76% above its $169 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $87.01\u2013$300 range.","pros":["Revenue grew 52.0%/yr over 5y","27 analysts' mean target $358 (+21%)","12-1 month momentum +16%","Operating margin expanding 1.1%/yr"],"cons":["Trades 76% above fair value of $169","Net debt/EBITDA 3.1x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","EV/EBITDA 14.5x vs sector 10.5x","P/FCF 64.2x vs sector 15.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["its co